{
  "_comment": [
    "Synthetic benchmark corpus. Every name, address, number, key and domain",
    "below was invented for this file or taken from a reserved example range",
    "(.invalid, 555 numbers, AWS's documented placeholder key); none of it is",
    "derived from a real person or account.",
    "",
    "A record is a list of chunks. A plain string is background text; a",
    "[label, text] pair is an expected finding; an optional third element is an",
    "entity key, and chunks sharing a key are mentions of the same person or",
    "thing. Offsets are computed from the chunks at load time, so re-wording a",
    "record cannot leave stale ground truth behind.",
    "",
    "Tiers: 'plain' is well-formed PII any working model should get; 'hard' is",
    "where exports and models are expected to diverge -- ambiguous names,",
    "unusual formats, entities mentioned more than once; 'clean' records are",
    "annotated as containing nothing, and any finding in them is a false alarm.",
    "The clean records avoid bare log timestamps and IP addresses on purpose:",
    "models with a finer taxonomy label those, and that is a vocabulary",
    "difference rather than a false positive."
  ],
